// `#Codable(published)` pins the struct's wire shape. The sibling
// .published.snapshot is the prior shape, which had no `verified`; adding
// the field with no migration to supply its value for data already written
// is E0910, reported at the marker that publishes the record (its span
// covers the whole `#Codable(published)`).
#Codable(published) Account: struct {
    name: String,
    verified: Bool,
}

run: fn() {
    a: Account{name: "Alice", verified: true}
    print("{a.name}")
}
